# FMCG changes include bakery

Most of Joy Superbakers is the FMCG manufacturer product. Her template is `fmcg-bakery`. A new FMCG feature or update applies to bakery in the same change, unless it is production.

| Org | Org id | Template | What she keeps |
|---|---|---|---|
| Top Food Ea Ltd | `org-top-food-ea-ltd` | `fmcg-manufacturer` | FMCG plant, including production: blend formula, blend / production run |
| Joy Superbakers ltd | `org-sfa-6a890b7765042fb41c9d89a6` | `fmcg-bakery` | Same FMCG selling and operations. Her own production: recipe, production batch |

## Do this on every FMCG change

- Customers, products, departments, price lists, tax tags, dispatch, orders, approvals, navigation, and permissions on those screens are shared.
- Put `fmcg-bakery` on the same gate as `fmcg-manufacturer`. Use `FMCG_SELLING_TEMPLATE_IDS`.
- `bakex` and `bakery` resolve to `fmcg-bakery`. That id is the bakery production path. It is not the company Bakex Millers.
- Do not copy an FMCG screen into a second bakery implementation.
- Do not ship an FMCG selling or operations change that only `fmcg-manufacturer` can see.

## Leave these alone

- Production wording and modules stay on each template. Do not give Joy blend / production run. Do not give Top Food recipe / production batch.
- Leave `fmcg-manufacturer` terminology as Top Food's FMCG plant.
- `seed-fmcg-manufacturing.ts` must leave a bakery org on `fmcg-bakery`.

